WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.640
- Law school is really expensive.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.990
And it's easy to assume
that the only good resources

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.370
in law school are also really expensive,

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.010
but that's simply not the case.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.650
Today, we're gonna talk
about the free resources

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.550
that you should be using to supercharge

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.971
your law school education
and get better grades.

00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:20.638
(bright instrumental music)

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.730
The first free resource

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.366
that I would recommend in
law school is called Anki.

00:00:26.366 --> 00:00:29.277
Anki is a digital flash card software.

00:00:29.277 --> 00:00:31.930
Simply put, there is no better way

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.640
to help you memorize things.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.810
Paper flash cards get a bad rap,

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.870
and part of that is deserved.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.160
But there's been a lot of
research into the science

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.100
of memorizing things
over the last 20 years.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.440
Recently, study after study has shown

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.910
that something called
spaced repetition learning

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.740
can supercharge your
ability to recall things.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.940
The basis of the system is simple.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.470
The more you remember something,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.070
the less you need to study it.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.170
The less you remember it,

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.740
the more often you need
to see the flashcard.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.860
Anki has this kind of periodization

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.166
or spaced repetition built into it.

00:01:04.166 --> 00:01:07.210
It's been used by language
learners for years.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.830
It allows people to learn
entire languages in just months.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.340
In fact, I'm using it to
learn Japanese right now.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.250
So, for example, if I am
displayed a flashcard,

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.830
and I get the answer right,
then I tell the software

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.040
that I got that card right,

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.620
and I won't see that card again for a day.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.320
But if I got the card wrong,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.040
then I'll see that card
again within one minute.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.980
I'll keep seeing it until
I get that card right.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.300
This system is the fastest
way to remember things,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.400
like elements of a cause of action

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.560
or memorizing the facts
of a particular case.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.840
If you use visual cues
like pictures or mnemonics,

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.110
you can really supercharge

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.630
your ability to learn
these concepts really fast.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.010
Not everything that you need
to learn for final exams

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.050
is conductive to being memorized
via flashcards like Anki,

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.230
but I say that at least 80% is.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.280
If you wanna memorize things
in the minimum amount of time,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.060
use Anki or another spaced
repetition flashcard system.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.900
It is a great system.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.480
Very few people use it,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.830
and it is perfectly free on a laptop.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.257
The next free resource that
I would use is Westlaw.

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:15.070
Westlaw is not just the
thing that you have to use

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.210
in your legal writing and research class.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:21.230
It's also a wonderful tool for
shortcutting your study time.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.540
Lawyers are very lazy.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.330
They are willing to pay a
ton of money to have things

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.940
spoonfed to them, and Westlaw
and LexisNexis fill that need.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.460
Every American case is reported

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.770
and analyzed by an army of lawyers.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.610
Here at Legal Eagle, we
recommend commercial outlines

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.730
and case summary services like Quimbee,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.010
but you can get 90% of the benefit

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.260
of those things straight
from Westlaw itself.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.690
They summarize the facts,
and most importantly,

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.570
they give you the black letter law.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.070
Find what works best for
you and your professor,

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.813
between commercial
supplements and outlines,

00:02:57.813 --> 00:03:00.870
but don't forget the
West head notes as well

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.740
and read those first before
you dive into your case book.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.050
It will make your reading so much clearer,

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.010
save you headaches, and save you time.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.630
We go into this in more depth

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.450
in our Guide to Law School Cases.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.050
You can get a link to that down below.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.270
The third free resource you should use

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.640
is your law school librarian.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.470
Your law school librarians can help you

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.250
with just about anything:
writing assignments, research

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:27.000
assignments, law review
articles, just about anything.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.320
But the most important thing

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.820
that they can help you
with is practice tests.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.810
Unfortunately, law schools
tend to keep a tight lid

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.900
on their practice tests, so
they make it hard to find,

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.780
and they certainly don't advertise them.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.600
Your law librarians are the gatekeepers.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.440
They are your best resource
for finding prior exams

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.750
from your school, and,

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.023
most importantly, for
your particular professor.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.450
I talk about practice exams
a lot on this channel.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.580
It's one of the most important things

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.320
you can do to get better grades.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.790
So, go get them from your law librarians.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.350
Get as many as you can.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.160
Get exams from other professors.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.280
It doesn't matter.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.830
Just do them.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.350
Your grades will thank you.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.380
Okay, the next free resource
that I would recommend

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.190
in law school is Dropbox or Google Drive,

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.640
some sort of cloud storage system.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.920
Everyone has a horror story
about their laptop crashing

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.970
the night before a
writing assignment is due

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.130
or losing their outline just
before they started studying.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.570
All of your law school files
should be pretty small,

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.080
just Word documents, mainly.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.820
So sign up for a free Dropbox
or Google Drive account.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.170
Automatically save your
work to those folders,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.080
and while you're at it,

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.320
tell Word to auto save your
work every few seconds.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.970
Your peace of mind is
worth this free resource,

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:39.980
and there's just no
reason in this day and age

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.960
not to have some sort of cloud system.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.540
The next free resource I would recommend

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.379
is your school's gym.

00:04:45.379 --> 00:04:48.950
It's too easy to get completely
out of shape in law school.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.640
Thanks to the arms race
between colleges, odds are,

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.260
you have access to a
really nice gym on campus.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.270
And that probably includes classes

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.110
that are free to take at the gym.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.530
Part of doing well in law school

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.940
is staying mentally and physically fit.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.600
So don't neglect your gym,

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.580
and don't neglect your body
or your health as well.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.260
It's too easy to fall into
the trap of eating nothing

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.030
but junk food and just
studying all the time,

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.070
but in the long run, it is better for you

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.870
to stay mentally and physically
fit, and that requires

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.060
that you go to the gym
every once in a while.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.370
The next free resource you should

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.270
absolutely use in law
school is your professor.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.030
You should go to office hours.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.720
It is amazing how few people

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.330
actually go to the
professor's office hours.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.150
These people are experts in their field,

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.360
and more importantly, they're the ones

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.170
that are going to test
you on your final exam.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.400
So find out what they in particular

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.370
think about a certain section of law.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.090
Their version is more important
than any other resource.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:52.400
If your professor contradicts
a commercial supplement,

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.770
go with your professor.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.820
That's the version that's
going to be on the test.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.240
But you can use your
professor to clarify things

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.770
that you don't understand.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.630
If your professor offers
practice exams, do them,

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.690
and then talk about the practice
exam with your professor

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.210
and talk about what you can do better.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:11.500
Find out what you did wrong
and what you did right.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.830
Get to know the professor.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.570
Your professor is genuinely
interested in the law;

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.750
otherwise, they wouldn't be a professor.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.500
And hopefully, you are too.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.160
If so, talk shop.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.261
Go to office hours.

00:06:22.261 --> 00:06:25.840
Getting good grades is only
one way to get a good job.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:29.148
Remember that getting a
referral from your professor is

00:06:29.148 --> 00:06:33.750
another perfectly legitimate
way of getting a 1L or 2L job.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.310
So get to know the professor.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.040
Show some genuine interest,

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.650
and use them to build your network.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.650
Oh, and you know what else
will help you get better grades

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.830
